{"name":"Wild Wilderness","hex":"#91857c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"wilderness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Uncultivated and unsettled land in its natural state inhabited by wild animals and with vegetation growing wild;  a tract of such land; a waste or wild.","A place other than land (for example, the air or sea) that is uncared for, and therefore devoted to disorder or wildness.\n\n An ornamental part of a garden or park cultivated with trees and often a maze to evoke a natural wilderness.\n\n Unrefinedness; wildness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wilderness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wilderness","blocks":[{"text":"Wilderness or wildlands are Earth's natural environments that have not been significantly modified by human activity, or any nonurbanized land not under extensive agricultural cultivation. The term has traditionally referred to terrestrial environments, though growing attention is being placed on marine wilderness. Recent maps of wilderness suggest it covers roughly one-quarter of Earth's terrestrial surface, but is being rapidly degraded by human activity. Even less wilderness remains in the ocean, with only 13.2% free from intense human activity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg/330px-Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilderness","wikidata":"Q911871"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rockymountainnps_%281%29.jpg/500px-Rockymountainnps_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rockymountainnps_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Rockymountainnps_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rockymountainnps_%281%29.jpg/500px-Rockymountainnps_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White Goat Wilderness Area in Canadian Rockies, Canada.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARockymountainnps_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Little_Beaver_valley.jpg/500px-Little_Beaver_valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Little_Beaver_valley.jpg/1280px-Little_Beaver_valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Little_Beaver_valley.jpg/500px-Little_Beaver_valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stephen Mather Wilderness in the U.S. state of Washington.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALittle_Beaver_valley.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Innoko_Wilderness.jpg/500px-Innoko_Wilderness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Innoko_Wilderness.jpg/500px-Innoko_Wilderness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Innoko Wilderness in the 